{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp","id":172421,"title":"Demon: The Descent LARP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-17T21:55:39-07:00","id":172421,"title":"Demon: The Descent LARP","content":"Quick Question: Does anyone have any experience running a DtD LARP? Can any one think of any particular issues, problems or considerations arising from moving embeds, exploits, etc. into MET?<br /> <br /> Secondly, has anyone adapted or tried to adapt GMC to Mind's Eye Theatre?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T13:34:20-07:00","id":173111,"title":"","content":"I'd say the main issue is the fact, that covers change.. and you need to somehow be able to tell them apart. Other than that... hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:48:53-07:00","id":173332,"title":"","content":"My thought for that have multiple name tags that fit inside a <a href=\"http://www.staples.com/IDville-Clear-Vinyl-Horizontal-Event-Badge-Holder-With-Cord/product_206524\" target=\"_blank\">plastic holder</a>, having the covers name, physical description, and apparent profession/clothing, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:42:33-07:00","id":175209,"title":"","content":"Having read and played <i>Requiem</i> and read <i>Awakening,</i> my experience is that, in general, powers that affect wide swaths of people or areas of land, or that deal with spontaneous travel over anything bigger than a room, are the powers that get changed the most when it comes to the translation into MET. And both <i>Requiem</i> and <i>Awakening </i>have some nice sidebars on what changed and why.<br /> The primary problem I see with a Demon LARP is the simple fact that a lot of the Embeds/Exploits fall into the category of altering wides swaths of people, as they alter the observers perception's of the scene. Coupled with the fact that most of them also don't incur a Resistance... I can almost hear the whining now.<br /> I do like the idea of the plastic name-tag for Covers though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:20:27-07:00","id":233215,"title":"","content":"I was playing around with a Demon LARP (played Masquerade and Requiem LARP for several years). The Rules are rather easy imho. But the problem is the espionage and pact part. If you have a lot of people, some who play human, some who play angels and GM-Cultists, it would work fine. But as long as you have just 10 or 20 People to play, and everyone like to be a demon, I see no chance for a satisfying game.<br /> <br /> Vampire is lot easier because Vampires have an own society. You can always celebrate religions festivals, perform rituals, fight against the Covenant you do not like, save the Masquerade and judge People who violate the traditions.<br /> But Demons? What did you like to do on a session?<br /> \u201cMy name is Mr...\u201d<br /> \u201cPsst! No Names!\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, OK! I am a Guard...\u201d<br /> \u201cPsst! No personal information, the GM is everywhere!\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, OK! I... I... well, forget it!\u201d<br /> <br /> You just need people (mostly normal people) around the Demon for the full fun.<br /> <br /> I tried to solve that problem for weeks but I do not have a answer for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:52:37-07:00","id":236041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=233215#post233215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing around with a Demon LARP (played Masquerade and Requiem LARP for several years). The Rules are rather easy imho. But the problem is the espionage and pact part. If you have a lot of people, some who play human, some who play angels and GM-Cultists, it would work fine. But as long as you have just 10 or 20 People to play, and everyone like to be a demon, I see no chance for a satisfying game.<br /> <br /> Vampire is lot easier because Vampires have an own society. You can always celebrate religions festivals, perform rituals, fight against the Covenant you do not like, save the Masquerade and judge People who violate the traditions.<br /> But Demons? What did you like to do on a session?<br /> \u201cMy name is Mr...\u201d<br /> \u201cPsst! No Names!\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, OK! I am a Guard...\u201d<br /> \u201cPsst! No personal information, the GM is everywhere!\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, OK! I... I... well, forget it!\u201d<br /> <br /> You just need people (mostly normal people) around the Demon for the full fun.<br /> <br /> I tried to solve that problem for weeks but I do not have a answer for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've been trying to solve an imaginary problem where people keep shushing you for presenting names and personal details that are explicitly false and escapable and this has taken up<i> weeks</i> of thinking then I feel comfortable saying the issue is not on the game's end of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:50:43-07:00","id":236230,"title":"","content":"Phew! Excuse me, Satchel, English is not my first language. I understand the most but I am not sure what you want to say. Could you pleas repeat it with other words?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T00:20:24-07:00","id":236255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=236230#post236230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phew! Excuse me, Satchel, English is not my first language. I understand the most but I am not sure what you want to say. Could you pleas repeat it with other words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any sane game of Demon is not going to result in &quot;No names! No personal information!&quot; because 1) these are both aspects of demonic Covers - i.e. not aspects of the demon that the Machine is after, as well as capable of being instantly discarded by all but the weakest Unchained - and thus the bigger threat is having the wrong Cover be found somewhere it shouldn't be, 2) demons favor oblique, matter-of-fact terminology for precisely the reason that it's easy to play off compared to the poetic/occult terms other splats use in their respective patois, and 3) I can practically guarantee something with as big-picture a perspective as God's is not going to be monitoring conversations for words like &quot;guardian&quot; or &quot;wheel.&quot; (And even if it did, a) that's what codes are for and b) there are Embeds for the specific purpose of covertly sharing information or obscuring conversation.)<br /> <br /> In short, &quot;everybody shushes everybody for three hours&quot; is a rather poor game of espionage, techgnostic or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T00:53:43-07:00","id":236274,"title":"","content":"You are right, sure. That was just the most extreme example. The main problem is, that you need a lot of non-Demon Characters for a good Demon game. Who do you want to make pacts with? Who is your antagonist? All that is easy if you have a lot of people. In the moment you have just a few you have to ask, what a hand of Demons should do, not to become bored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T01:00:23-07:00","id":236279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=236274#post236274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, sure. That was just the most extreme example. The main problem is, that you need a lot of non-Demon Characters for a good Demon game. Who do you want to make pacts with? Who is your antagonist? All that is easy if you have a lot of people. In the moment you have just a few you have to ask, what a hand of Demons should do, not to become bored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute that, make 5 different agencies out of the 20 or so players and you'll see them fighting for resources even worse than vampires will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T02:10:13-07:00","id":236299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=236279#post236279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dispute that, make 5 different agencies out of the 20 or so players and you'll see them fighting for resources even worse than vampires will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. I would make a background history of the city explaining that after last big act against the God-machine they were hunted by not one, but three Angels. Everybody learned the lesson and grew extremely careful when it comes to interfere with infrastructures. The survivors founded an Agency (Les Cavaliers) to keep track of God-machine's activities and avoid as much as possible direct conflict. They observe every demon in the city and spy them to get to know their plains.<br /> <br /> During your games, they would be older and powerful demons, intercepting every move they think it's unwise. Also, they would use this excuse of protecting the city to maintain their status and grow in power, almost making a dictatorship.<br /> <br /> Add to this scenario a new Agency of Saboteurs, hungry to fight against the God-machine at any cost. Another Agency specialized in &quot;last minute pacts&quot; to desperated and hunted demons and also another agency who believes the right path is to force Angels to fall, playing a very dangerous game by talking to them or making their missions fail.<br /> <br /> There you go. You got plenty of plots for a Live Action who doesn't need a huge cast of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","user":"Amadeu","date":". 08-21-2014, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T04:21:17-07:00","id":236322,"title":"","content":"I still see some problems remain, but a Demon LARP becomes imaginable for me. I think the key is a lot of groundwork to create Agencys which are constantly fight about the same resources but share some goals as well. There is just one thing I could hardly imagine. How would you handle pacts? Because the fun about it is to outsmart the human. How do you do that with no one playing the human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T10:59:39-07:00","id":236692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=236322#post236322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How would you handle pacts? Because the fun about it is to outsmart the human. How do you do that with no one playing the human?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make them in between sections. This is not a theme for the night of the live action, this should be handled with an appropriate storyteller, before or after the big night.<br /> <br /> Step one would be defining which contacts the demon has. Does his cover has a profession? A family? Old friends?<br /> <br /> Step two, the storyteller would look at the demon's social and mental traits and make a roll based on how will this demon is trying to locate the appropriate &quot;victim&quot;. Will him go around spying on their lives to find their flaws and take note on hiw he could make it better? Will him seduce his victim with the lust of power, women, money or a new job promotion? Will him create a situation that the mortal would be forced to make a desperate pact?<br /> <br /> <br /> After analyzing this roll, the storyteller should provide the player a short list of mortals (no more than 3) with a few nice details based on the sucess of the test. Excepcional sucess will reveal the perfect victim or that specific person could even contact the demon in search for help.<br /> <br /> Step three, after finding the right victim, the storyteller would roleplay that person and set up if he will accept, deny or negociate the pact, based on how good the player can convince, intimidate or seduce.<br /> <br /> Step four, the storyteller records on a special sheet the pact, the victim's details and the terms of it.<br /> <br /> Done. I think imho that is very silly to have mortal players on this Live Action. They not just would have more fun role playing demons, but also as soon as they discover that their role on this scenario is just to make a pact and they are among players with a lot of powers that they don't have, I can picture them very pissed off. I would have a lot to explain to them off character! In a live action is crucial to have fair rules and make the most out of every character, everybody must be protagonist and antagonist to someone else. Remember the storyteller should not interfere that much and it would be boring as hell to have only the ST as an enemy.<br /> <br /> But these are my players, and I don't know if such an unfair environment would be fine with yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","user":"Amadeu","date":".  added a few details. 08-21-2014, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T15:31:20-08:00","id":407074,"title":"","content":"How about a mix of Live Action game and Table?<br /> Like two or more rings who only barely know each other, with geotagging apps to signal &quot;hot&quot; spots for GM activity, like infrastructure or Occult Matrixes coming toghether.<br /> <br /> All interaction with Humans would be done in Downtime like a VtR MET game and the live elements comes up only when the players Wish.<br /> With most contact done via IM, Forum Posts or something of sorts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5064-clonea85m09","name":"Clonea85m09","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:50:03-08:00","id":407287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clonea85m09</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp?p=407074#post407074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a mix of Live Action game and Table?<br /> Like two or more rings who only barely know each other, with geotagging apps to signal &quot;hot&quot; spots for GM activity, like infrastructure or Occult Matrixes coming toghether.<br /> <br /> All interaction with Humans would be done in Downtime like a VtR MET game and the live elements comes up only when the players Wish.<br /> <b>With most contact done via IM, Forum Posts or something of sorts</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're onto something with the bolded section. As an espionage game, the line between LARP and PBP could get extremely blurry in Demon. Add in a few ARG-ish elements and you've got a recipe for a hell of an epic game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:24:18-08:00","id":408487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/172421-demon-the-descent-larp#post172421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, has anyone adapted or tried to adapt GMC to Mind's Eye Theatre?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to use MET specific rules like capping damage or whatever that might be complicated but if all you want to do is be able to use cards as your randomizer so you can stand and walk around while rping then it's easy as pie to run the new GMC rules in a larp. If you change your <a href=\"http://larp.davisgames.com/wiki/index.php?title=Rules:NWoD:Card_Draw_Mechanic\" target=\"_blank\">success thresholds</a> like my group did then your expected successes will be close enough you can just run things from the TT book without issue.* Likewise you can just take Demon and run it with the swapped out randomizer.<br /> <br /> * You'll note we did make a few other changes to probability such as allowing for any test to Dramatically Fail, not just those reduced to 0 dice. Changeling the target successes alone is all it takes to run TT material in a larp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}